# Scoped, auto-expiring exceptions for the CRITICAL/HIGH vulnerability gate in
# .github/workflows/build-and-publish.yml. Keep this file empty unless a finding
# truly cannot be fixed by re-baking (for example a vendor-shipped static binary
# that only the vendor can rebuild). Every entry must carry an exp: date, name the
# binary it covers in a comment, and be removed as soon as the vendor ships a fix.
#
# Format:  CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# The Nsight Compute/Systems Go binaries that used to live here are no longer
# installed; the image ships the CUDA compiler, dev libraries and command-line
# tools instead of the full cuda-toolkit metapackage.

# nvidia-container-toolkit 1.20.1-1 is the newest release in both NVIDIA apt repos
# (checked 2026-10-10) and is built with Go 1.27.1; these three Go stdlib HIGH
# denial-of-service CVEs (net/http Range parsing, HTTP/2 SETTINGS flooding, crypto/tls
# ECH extension handling) are fixed in Go 1.27.2 and only an NVIDIA rebuild clears
# them. They are reported against /usr/bin/nvidia-ctk, nvidia-cdi-hook,
# nvidia-container-runtime and nvidia-container-runtime-hook, none of which serves
# HTTP or TLS. Remove as soon as a toolkit built with Go >= 1.27.2 ships; the gate
# goes red again when they expire.
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2026-11-20
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-11-20
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-11-20
